                <pb facs="0321" n="312" sameAs="frus:frus1940v02/pg312"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.C1/133: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in the
                        Netherlands</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gordon</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-02-06T15:00:00-05:00">February 6, 1940—3
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>17. A committee appointed by the Assembly of the League of Nations to inaugurate
                    a plan for the reorganization of the League’s technical work will meet at The
                    Hague beginning February 7. For your strictly confidential information, the
                    Department has not yet determined the attitude it will adopt toward the new
                    organization and would prefer not to be approached on the subject at this
                    time.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
